  "descriptionMarkdown": "Displays a value as a [Cistertian numeral](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cistercian_numerals).\n\nThe input is the constant provider on top, but it can be replaced by any circuit value. Change the item you want to filter for in the arithmetic combinator under the constant provider.\n\nWhat you get is a value between 0 and 9999 as a Cistertian numeral. It's less space-efficient than a binary representation, but might be easier to read. Two in a row and an another trivial arithmetic combinator gets you numbers up to 999,999.",
